ere rotten, and the rest were petrified. I said \u201cpetrified\u201d was a good word. I believed that the only proper way to sort the great ages of some of those jokes was by geological periods. But that clever idea hit the boy in a blank spot, because geology hadn\u2019t been invented yet. Still, I made a note of his remark and figured I could educate the commonwealth up to it if I made it through. There\u2019s no point throwing away a good thing just because the market isn\u2019t ready.\\n\\nNow Sir Kay stood up and started firing at me with his history-mill, using me as fuel.\"}"
